# Which model to run. Part 3 = change this line. One file per option in config/:
#   fast       qwen3.7-flash via OpenRouter  (recommended: fastest, cheapest, most reliable)
#   openrouter qwen3-32b via OpenRouter
#   openai     gpt-5-mini
MODEL=fast

# --- the one key you need to add ---------------------------------------------
# Billable, so it has to be yours: openrouter.ai/keys. A few dollars of credit
# covers far more than a demo.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# --- already filled in, on purpose -------------------------------------------
# A working trade.gov key is committed here so this repo runs with one key
# instead of two. It is free, read-only and not billable: it buys queries
# against the public Consolidated Screening List and nothing else. There is no
# account, quota or spend behind it to protect, and getting your own means a
# second signup on a separate developer portal — friction with no security
# gained. Rotating it is a click, so it is shared knowingly, not carelessly.
#
# The contrast is the point: keys that cost money or carry an identity stay
# empty above and below. Free public-data keys are not the same class of thing.
TRADE_GOV_API_KEY=fd1fa8af86e849f3b379debfab9ebd19

# --- optional ----------------------------------------------------------------
OPENAI_API_KEY=                # only for MODEL=openai
OLLAMA_API_KEY=ollama          # any value; Ollama ignores it
